// ADX-Filtered Trend
//
// A moving-average crossover that only trades when Wilder's ADX says a trend actually
// exists. Below 20, ADX is telling you the market is ranging and a crossover means little.
//
// The point of including it is comparative: run it beside "MA Crossover" and the filter's
// value shows up as fewer trades, not as a better win rate. Whether that is worth it is an
// expectancy question, which is what the scorecard answers.
strategy("ADX-Filtered Trend", overlay = true)

fast = ema(close, 20)
slow = ema(close, 50)
[adxv, plusDi, minusDi] = adx(14)

trending = adxv > 20

plot(fast, title = "Fast", color = color.accent)
plot(slow, title = "Slow", color = color.mute)

if crossover(fast, slow) and trending
    strategy.entry("filtered", strategy.long)

if crossunder(fast, slow)
    strategy.close("filtered")
